<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wilfrid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 633–709</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Saint Wilfrid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wilfrid was a Northumbrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> and saint who championed Roman church practice at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/synod-of-whitby">Synod of Whitby</a> in 664 and became Bishop of York. Repeatedly expelled after quarrels with kings and archbishops, he appealed twice to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, and during one exile he converted the South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> in the 680s and founded a monastery at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/selsey">Selsey</a>. He also founded monasteries at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ripon">Ripon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hexham">Hexham</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Royal power depended heavily on the church: kings founded and endowed monasteries, and bishops such as <b>Wilfrid of York</b>, Cuthbert of Lindisfarne and Ecgberht of York were political figures in their own right.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-northumbria">Kingdom of Northumbria · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Its first known king, Aldgisl, sheltered the English bishop <b>Wilfrid</b> in 678.</blockquote><a href="/state/frisian-kingdom">Frisian Kingdom</a></li><li><blockquote>Paganism lasted until <b>Wilfrid of York</b> converted the South Saxons in the 680s, founding a monastery at Selsey on land given by King Aethelwealh; Selsey later became the seat of the South Saxon bishopric.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-sussex">Kingdom of Sussex</a></li><li><blockquote>The island became part of Wessex and was converted by <b>Wilfrid's</b> clergy.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-the-isle-of-wight">Kingdom of the Isle of Wight</a></li></ul></section>
